.TH FIOMARK 1 "September 2026" "fiomark 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fiomark \- CrystalDiskMark-style storage benchmark driven by fio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fiomark
[\fB\-\-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-size\fR \fIGiB\fR] [\fB\-\-runtime\fR \fISECONDS\fR] [\fB\-\-start\fR]
.br
.B fiomark \-\-cli
[\fB\-\-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-size\fR \fIGiB\fR] [\fB\-\-runtime\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fiomark
measures a filesystem's storage performance by running a fixed suite of
.BR fio (1)
jobs against a test file it creates in the chosen directory: sequential 1 MiB transfers at
queue depth 8, random 4 KiB transfers at queue depth 32 with four jobs, and random 4 KiB
transfers at queue depth 1, each as a read pass and a write pass. All jobs use direct I/O and the
io_uring engine. Results are shown as MB/s with IOPS and mean completion latency.
.PP
Without options a window opens. With
.B \-\-cli
the same suite runs in the terminal and prints a table; no display is required.
.PP
The test file is removed when the run finishes, is stopped, or fails. fiomark refuses to start
without write permission or enough free space, and warns when the target is ZFS or tmpfs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " PATH"
Directory in which to create the test file. Default: the home directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " GiB"
Size of the test file. Default: 4.
.TP
.BI \-\-runtime " SECONDS"
Duration of each of the six tests. Default: 15.
.TP
.B \-\-start
Begin the run as soon as the window opens (ignored with \fB\-\-cli\fR, which always starts).
.TP
.B \-\-cli
Run in the terminal and print a results table.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage for the terminal mode.
.SH EXIT STATUS
In terminal mode, 0 on success and 1 if the run failed or could not start.
.SH NOTES
Write passes add some tens of gigabytes of wear per run on fast drives. On laptops, run on mains
power. Results on copy-on-write or caching filesystems include the filesystem's own behaviour.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fio (1),
.BR lsblk (8),
.BR nvme (1)
